      "content": "While electrolyte imbalance can cause thirst, the specific combination of symptoms you described suggests a need for a medical evaluation, not just a sugary drink. While Gatorade or Liquid IV might temporarily quench thirst, they won't address the underlying cause if it's related to blood sugar. Since you can't see a doctor right away, try keeping a detailed log of your symptoms and water intake, and perhaps try a low-sugar electrolyte solution until you can get professional advice.",
